1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
WWW.MY-SUBS.CO

1
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:11,260
Papa, I've looked at the estate accounts

2
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:15,130
and if we all learned to dress ourselves,
we could save 40,000 a year.

3
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:17,520
Next you'll be suggesting you go and get a job.

4
00:00:18,588 --> 00:00:19,811
Oh, I do so love Christmas.

5
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:21,322
The whole family together.

6
00:00:21,322 --> 00:00:23,320
It's a pity Granny decided to go skiing.

7
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:25,320
She was in the papers today.

8
00:00:25,463 --> 00:00:28,141
She's broken the world record for ski jump.

9
00:00:29,331 --> 00:00:30,112
Good for her.

10
00:00:30,776 --> 00:00:33,647
Though I must say I've never been happier,
and long may it last.

11
00:00:34,141 --> 00:00:35,640
A toast to happiness.

12
00:00:35,985 --> 00:00:37,632
- To happiness.
- Happiness.

13
00:00:38,061 --> 00:00:39,630
Telegram, my lord.

14
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:40,997
Thank you, Carson.

15
00:00:44,084 --> 00:00:45,600
- Ohh.
- Bad news?

16
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,054
I'm afraid so.

17
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:49,416
It appears I have lost our entire fortune.

18
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:50,061
Not again.

19
00:00:50,061 --> 00:00:52,060
I've let you all down.

20
00:00:53,035 --> 00:00:55,510
Frankly, it would be better if I had never been born.

21
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:56,536
Darling, don't say that.

22
00:00:56,536 --> 00:00:58,530
I'm going to take the car out for a spin.

23
00:00:59,256 --> 00:00:59,934
Papa, don't.

24
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:03,425
You know what happens to anyone who takes the car out for a spin at Christmas.

25
00:01:03,703 --> 00:01:04,070
Quite.

26
00:01:04,621 --> 00:01:06,169
I may be some time.

27
00:01:11,364 --> 00:01:13,416
Don't be ridiculous, Lord Grantham.

28
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:14,960
You have everything to live for.

29
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:16,574
Crikey, who are you?

30
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:17,854
I'm an angel, darling.

31
00:01:18,734 --> 00:01:21,369
Look, I want to show you what life would have been like here

32
00:01:21,369 --> 00:01:23,360
If indeed you had never been born.

33
00:01:25,675 --> 00:01:29,388
This will be perfect for when I'm doing the Black Bottom at the Tea Dance.

34
00:01:29,868 --> 00:01:33,350
This will be perfect for when I'm on stage with my band.

35
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:34,607
Ahh, you got my delivery.

36
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:37,581
Is that a tradesman? In one of the bedrooms?

37
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,341
Yes. He's rather dishy.

38
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:41,708
That's right, ladies. All the way from Selfridge's

39
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:44,795
I brought you the finest in silk undergarments.

40
00:01:44,922 --> 00:01:45,623
Typical yank.

41
00:01:45,882 --> 00:01:46,781
Harry?

42
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:48,282
What are you doing here?

43
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,689
I brought you this.

44
00:01:50,122 --> 00:01:53,454
Ohh, are you buying Mr. Selfridge's undergarments, too?

45
00:01:53,496 --> 00:01:56,650
Well, not as such, but last time I was in Mr. Selfridge's store

46
00:01:56,650 --> 00:02:00,047
We were discussing how to help the poor at the east end,

47
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:03,374
and somehow, I managed to leave it in his office.

48
00:02:04,517 --> 00:02:05,534
It's easily done.

49
00:02:06,687 --> 00:02:07,322
Isobelle.

50
00:02:07,783 --> 00:02:10,517
In a bedroom with a tradesman? With a beard?

51
00:02:10,517 --> 00:02:12,510
He is one of the richest men in England.

52
00:02:12,936 --> 00:02:13,458
Is he.

53
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:15,416
Perhaps he should meet Edith.

54
00:02:15,623 --> 00:02:16,771
What is going on here?

55
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,576
I think you need to leave. Now.

56
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:22,889
Come, come. Downton Abbey and Mr. Selfridge should not be quarreling.

57
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,298
After all, we are on the same channel.

58
00:02:25,290 --> 00:02:29,891
Ahh, and this will be perfect when I'm being flighty and spontaneous.

59
00:02:30,004 --> 00:02:30,691
That's right.

60
00:02:31,044 --> 00:02:33,458
That is the spirit, and there is more of that at Selfridge's

61
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:37,416
Because it is a wonderful, magical place where all your dreams could come true,

62
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:40,560
And the only limit is your imagination.

63
00:02:41,011 --> 00:02:41,938
You're not Willy Wonka.

64
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:42,847
Not yet.

65
00:02:42,847 --> 00:02:44,840
Do you have these in a size

66
00:02:44,997 --> 00:02:45,647
Thirteen?

67
00:02:46,992 --> 00:02:47,576
Come, come.

68
00:02:47,727 --> 00:02:48,545
I think it's time.

69
00:02:52,268 --> 00:02:54,367
His lordship's whiskey is absolutely delicious.

70
00:02:54,644 --> 00:02:56,522
Not as nice as his brandy.

71
00:02:56,578 --> 00:02:57,538
This is disgraceful.

72
00:02:57,901 --> 00:02:59,247
What, them nicking your booze?

73
00:02:59,312 --> 00:03:00,611
I don't care about the booze.

74
00:03:00,969 --> 00:03:02,592
Look at that fool Carson.

75
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,174
He's wearing my best slippers.

76
00:03:04,192 --> 00:03:04,861
I'm out.

77
00:03:08,658 --> 00:03:09,444
Three kings.

78
00:03:12,169 --> 00:03:13,854
Not so fast, buster.

79
00:03:15,341 --> 00:03:15,990
Full house.

80
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,576
Ladies over sevens.

81
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,858
Take them off.

82
00:03:21,938 --> 00:03:24,004
Off! Off! Off! Off!

83
00:03:27,915 --> 00:03:31,957
We don't want Mr. Molesley taking any more clothes off.

84
00:03:31,957 --> 00:03:33,950
Where's Jimmy when you need him.

85
00:03:38,508 --> 00:03:41,336
Why is Mrs. Patmore wearing those ludicrous glasses?

86
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:42,738
Because you don't exist

87
00:03:42,730 --> 00:03:45,204
The new earl hasn't paid for her cataract operation.

88
00:03:45,204 --> 00:03:47,200
Who is the new earl?

89
00:04:04,145 --> 00:04:05,298
What you making, Molesley?

90
00:04:05,336 --> 00:04:06,343
I'm busy.

91
00:04:10,616 --> 00:04:12,367
- What are you drinking, Rose?
- Busy.

92
00:04:14,263 --> 00:04:14,781
Thank you.

93
00:04:15,604 --> 00:04:16,635
Dearest.

94
00:04:16,941 --> 00:04:19,872
Lord and Lady Carlisle have asked us over for dinner tonight.

95
00:04:22,621 --> 00:04:23,552
Aww, heck.

